// Drive the PoS **delegation** path from a deploy, and report the result on a public name.
//
// `rho:rchain:pos!("delegate", *deployerId, operatorPubKey, amount, *ret)` moves the principal out of
// the **deployer's own** REV vault and adds it to the operator's `pos:bonds` entry, so the operator's
// key carries the **aggregate** of its own stake and every delegation to it (law 57, #193, and
// `spec/RUST-FIRST.md` § *Delegated stake*).
//
// **The delegator is the deployer**, and that is the whole of the authorisation: the unforgeable
// `*deployerId` is what spends the vault, exactly as `bond`'s is, so there is no program-authored way
// to delegate someone else's REV. The operator is the **named** key — a `ByteArray`, not the caller —
// which is what makes this a delegation rather than a self-bond.
//
// **The operator key below is a placeholder.** A devnet's validator keys are generated per run, so
// `spec/audit/evidence/n193-delegation-live-run.sh` substitutes the real one out of the genesis bonds
// file and deploys the substituted copy; what is checked in is the call shape, so the interface is
// reviewable without running anything.
//
// Publish the `(Bool, Either)` result so `tools/devnet.sh query pos-delegate` can read it back.
new pos(`rho:rchain:pos`), deployerId(`rho:rchain:deployerId`), ret in {
  pos!("delegate", *deployerId, "<OPERATOR_PUBKEY_HEX>".hexToBytes(), 40, *ret) |
  for (@result <- ret) {
    @"pos-delegate"!(result)
  }
}
